---
/*
 * The idea the home story has just shown, said once in plain words: the agents do the work and
 * the person only makes the decisions. It answers the hero's "Stop babysitting your agents."
 */
---

<section class="principle page reveal">
  <h2 class="section-title">Stop working for your agents. Let them work for you.</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    They split the work, finish it across your machines, and come to you only for the decisions.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .principle {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: 20px;
    padding-top: var(--section);
    text-align: center;
  }

  h2 {
    max-width: 13em;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.4vw, 52px);
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 30em;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
</style>
